# StudyBrain — App Review & Improvement Roadmap

## Current State ✅
The core loop works well: create lesson → upload docs → stream AI chat → persist to localStorage.
Fonts, dark theme, mobile layout, and PDF parsing are all solid.

---

## 🔴 Bugs / Critical Gaps

| # | Issue | Impact |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | **No Stop button** — once streaming starts, you can't cancel it | High |
| 2 | **localStorage ~5 MB limit** — large PDFs will silently fail or corrupt the store | High |
| 3 | **Lesson can't be renamed** — only create/delete, no edit | Medium |
| 4 | **No error retry** — if the AI call fails, the empty bubble just sits there with no way to retry | Medium |
| 5 | **Copy button missing** — can't copy an AI response to clipboard | Medium |

---

## 🟡 High-Value Features to Add

### 1. ⏹ Stop / Abort Streaming *(effort: small)*
Add a **Stop** button that replaces the Send button while the AI is typing.
Use `AbortController` to cancel the fetch mid-stream.

### 2. 📋 Copy Message Button *(effort: small)*
On hover/tap of any AI message, show a copy icon.
`navigator.clipboard.writeText(msg.content)` with a brief "Copied!" toast.

### 3. ✏️ Rename Lesson *(effort: small)*
Double-click or pencil icon on the lesson name → inline edit → Enter to save.

### 4. 🗑️ Clear Chat History *(effort: small)*
Button in the topbar (trash icon) to wipe just the chat, keeping docs intact.
Useful for starting a fresh conversation on the same material.

### 5. 🔍 Lesson Search in Sidebar *(effort: small)*
A tiny search input at the top of the sidebar to filter lessons by name.
Essential once you have 10+ lessons.

### 6. 🧠 AI Model Selector *(effort: medium)*
Dropdown in the lesson topbar to swap between models on OpenRouter:
- `anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-5` (current)
- `google/gemini-2.5-pro`
- `openai/gpt-4o`
- `meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct` (free)

Stored per-lesson in localStorage.

### 7. 📤 Export Chat as Markdown *(effort: small)*
"Export" button that downloads the chat history as a `.md` file.
Extremely useful for students who want to save notes.

### 8. 🃏 Flashcard Mode *(effort: medium)*
A "Flashcard" tab inside each lesson.
Sends a structured prompt to generate `[Term] → [Definition]` pairs from docs.
Renders them as flip cards with keyboard navigation (← →, Space to flip).

### 9. 📊 Doc Preview Drawer *(effort: medium)*
Clicking a doc chip opens a side drawer showing the raw extracted text.
Helps users verify the parsed content is correct (especially for PDFs).

### 10. 🏷️ Lesson Color Labels *(effort: tiny)*
Color dot picker on each lesson (6 preset colors).
Makes it easier to visually organize subjects in the sidebar.

---

